IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc15-rules.l4 -- sections 482 and 482.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XIV, Jurisdiction, "Rules of Court"):
-- the courts that may make rules of court and what the rules cover and reach (s 482), publication of the rules, uniform rules made by the Governor in Council,
-- and case management (s 482.1): the parties' duty to comply with a direction, the summons or warrant to compel the accused's presence, and the provisions that apply to it.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Imports the core only (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: see the head of ccc15-general.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc15)"):
-- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE.
-- Rule-making powers are machinery (the brief's reason 2 for inert), but they are the source of the rules that apply to the accused's own case, so they are encoded here for what they decide:
-- who may make rules, what the rules reach, what they cover, and what follows for the accused.

§ `Section 482(1) -- Power to make rules`

-- The courts are as s 2 says (inputs: the answers of `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` and `s 2 court of appeal`). Rules inconsistent with an Act are outside the grant.
-- src:8669 | Rules of Court
-- src:8670 | Power to make rules
-- src:8671 | 482 (1) Every superior court of criminal jurisdiction and every court of appeal may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament, and any rules so made apply to any prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal, as the case may be, within the jurisdiction of that court, instituted in relation to any matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to any such prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal.
@ref s 482(1) (src:8669-8671)
GIVEN `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 court of appeal: the court is a court of appeal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the rules are not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 court of appeal: the court is a court of appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN IF `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 2 court of appeal: the court is a court of appeal` EQUALS NOTHING
                 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the court is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of appeal is for s 2 and is not determined
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every superior court of criminal jurisdiction and every court of appeal may make rules of court"
        IF NOT `the rules are not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The effect of subsection (1): the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal. "So made" is the answer of the power above.
@ref s 482(1) (src:8671)
GIVEN `the rules were made under subsection (1), by s 482(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal is within the jurisdiction of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the rules were made under subsection (1), by s 482(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the rules were made under the power is not determined
        IF `the rules were made under subsection (1), by s 482(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any rules so made apply"
        IF NOT `the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal is within the jurisdiction of that court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the jurisdiction of that court"
        IF NOT `it is instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal of that kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "instituted in relation to any matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to any such prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 482(2) -- Power to make rules`

-- The list of courts is of courts that "may" make rules and does not say "only": another court is NOT COVERED.
-- src:8672 | Power to make rules
-- src:8673 | (2) The following courts may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament that are applicable to any prosecution, proceeding, including a preliminary inquiry or proceedings within the meaning of Part XXVII, action or appeal, as the case may be, within the jurisdiction of that court, instituted in relation to any matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal:
-- src:8674 | (a) every court of criminal jurisdiction for a province;
-- src:8675 | (b) every appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1);
-- src:8676 | (c) the Ontario Court of Justice;
-- src:8677 | (d) the Court of Quebec and every municipal court in the Province of Quebec;
-- src:8678 | (e) the Provincial Court of Nova Scotia;
-- src:8679 | (f) the Provincial Court of New Brunswick;
-- src:8680 | (g) the Provincial Court of Manitoba;
-- src:8681 | (h) the Provincial Court of British Columbia;
-- src:8682 | (i) the Provincial Court of Prince Edward Island;
-- src:8683 | (j) the Provincial Court of Saskatchewan;
-- src:8684 | (k) the Provincial Court of Alberta;
-- src:8685 | (l) the Provincial Court of Newfoundland and Labrador;
-- src:8686 | (m) the Territorial Court of Yukon;
-- src:8687 | (n) the Territorial Court of the Northwest Territories; and
-- src:8688 | (o) the Nunavut Court of Justice.
@ref s 482(2) (src:8672-8688)
DECLARE `s 482(2) the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province`
    `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)`
    `s 482(2)(c) the Ontario Court of Justice`
    `s 482(2)(d) the Court of Quebec`
    `s 482(2)(d) a municipal court in the Province of Quebec`
    `s 482(2)(e) the Provincial Court of Nova Scotia`
    `s 482(2)(f) the Provincial Court of New Brunswick`
    `s 482(2)(g) the Provincial Court of Manitoba`
    `s 482(2)(h) the Provincial Court of British Columbia`
    `s 482(2)(i) the Provincial Court of Prince Edward Island`
    `s 482(2)(j) the Provincial Court of Saskatchewan`
    `s 482(2)(k) the Provincial Court of Alberta`
    `s 482(2)(l) the Provincial Court of Newfoundland and Labrador`
    `s 482(2)(m) the Territorial Court of Yukon`
    `s 482(2)(n) the Territorial Court of the Northwest Territories`
    `s 482(2)(o) the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    `s 482(2) another court that no paragraph names`

@ref s 482(2) (src:8672-8688)
GIVEN court IS A `s 482(2) the court`
      `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 812 the court is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is a court referred to in subsection (1), by s 482(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the rules are not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2) another court that no paragraph names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following courts may make rules of court" does not say "only"
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` AND `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the court is a court of criminal jurisdiction is for s 2 and is not determined
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` AND NOT (`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every court of criminal jurisdiction for a province"
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` AND (`s 812 the court is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the court is a court referred to in subsection (1), by s 482(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the court is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812, or a court referred to in subsection (1), is not determined
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` AND `s 812 the court is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every appeal court within the meaning of section 812"
        IF court EQUALS `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` AND `the court is a court referred to in subsection (1), by s 482(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)" (a court of subsection (1) is outside paragraph (b): fork: other-than)
        IF NOT `the rules are not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 482(2) (src:8673)
GIVEN `the rules were made under subsection (2), by s 482(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal is within the jurisdiction of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the rules were made under subsection (2), by s 482(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the rules were made under the power is not determined
        IF `the rules were made under subsection (2), by s 482(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament that are applicable to any prosecution, proceeding"
        IF NOT `the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal is within the jurisdiction of that court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the jurisdiction of that court"
        IF NOT `it is instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal of that kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "instituted in relation to any matter of a criminal nature or arising from or incidental to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 482(3) -- Purpose of rules`

-- The purposes for which rules under subsection (1) or (2) may be made: a table, one constructor for each paragraph and subparagraph, and one for a purpose no paragraph names.
-- src:8689 | Purpose of rules
-- src:8690 | (3) Rules under subsection (1) or (2) may be made
-- src:8691 | (a) generally to regulate the duties of the officers of the court and any other matter considered expedient to attain the ends of justice and carry into effect the provisions of the law;
-- src:8692 | (b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers, except in so far as they are regulated by law;
-- src:8693 | (c) to regulate the pleading, practice and procedure in criminal matters, including pre-hearing conferences held under section 625.1, proceedings with respect to judicial interim release and preliminary inquiries and, in the case of rules under subsection (1), proceedings with respect to mandamus, certiorari, habeas corpus, prohibition and procedendo and proceedings on an appeal under section 830; and
-- src:8694 | (d) to carry out the provisions of this Act relating to appeals from conviction, acquittal or sentence and, without restricting the generality of this paragraph,
-- src:8695 | (i) for furnishing necessary forms and instructions in relation to notices of appeal or applications for leave to appeal to officials or other persons requiring or demanding them,
-- src:8696 | (ii) for ensuring the accuracy of notes taken at a trial and the verification of any copy or transcript,
-- src:8697 | (iii) for keeping writings, exhibits or other things connected with the proceedings on the trial,
-- src:8698 | (iv) for securing the safe custody of property during the period in which the operation of an order with respect to that property is suspended under subsection 689(1), and
-- src:8699 | (v) for providing that the Attorney General and counsel who acted for the Attorney General at the trial be supplied with certified copies of writings, exhibits and things connected with the proceedings that are required for the purposes of their duties.
@ref s 482(3) (src:8689-8699)
DECLARE `s 482(3) the purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 482(3)(a) generally to regulate the duties of the officers of the court and any other matter considered expedient to attain the ends of justice and carry into effect the provisions of the law`
    `s 482(3)(b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers`
    `s 482(3)(c) to regulate the pleading, practice and procedure in criminal matters, including pre-hearing conferences held under section 625.1, proceedings with respect to judicial interim release and preliminary inquiries`
    `s 482(3)(c) in the case of rules under subsection (1), proceedings with respect to mandamus, certiorari, habeas corpus, prohibition and procedendo and proceedings on an appeal under section 830`
    `s 482(3)(d) to carry out the provisions of this Act relating to appeals from conviction, acquittal or sentence`
    `s 482(3)(d)(i) furnishing necessary forms and instructions in relation to notices of appeal or applications for leave to appeal to officials or other persons requiring or demanding them`
    `s 482(3)(d)(ii) ensuring the accuracy of notes taken at a trial and the verification of any copy or transcript`
    `s 482(3)(d)(iii) keeping writings, exhibits or other things connected with the proceedings on the trial`
    `s 482(3)(d)(iv) securing the safe custody of property during the period in which the operation of an order with respect to that property is suspended under subsection 689(1)`
    `s 482(3)(d)(v) providing that the Attorney General and counsel who acted for the Attorney General at the trial be supplied with certified copies of writings, exhibits and things connected with the proceedings that are required for the purposes of their duties`
    `s 482(3) another purpose`

DECLARE `s 482(3) the subsection under which the rules are made` IS ONE OF
    `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)`
    `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)`

@ref s 482(3) (src:8689-8699)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 482(3) the purpose`
      `the subsection under which the rules are made` IS A `s 482(3) the subsection under which the rules are made`
      `the sittings are regulated by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 482(3) another purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) generally to regulate the duties of the officers of the court and any other matter considered expedient" and (b) to (d) do not say "only"
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 482(3)(b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers` AND `the sittings are regulated by law` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as they are regulated by law" (an exception that is met)
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 482(3)(c) in the case of rules under subsection (1), proceedings with respect to mandamus, certiorari, habeas corpus, prohibition and procedendo and proceedings on an appeal under section 830` AND `the subsection under which the rules are made` EQUALS `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of rules under subsection (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 482(4) and (5) -- Publication; uniform rules`

-- The text names no one who must publish the rules: no actor is invented (fork: bare-must),
-- so this is a decision function. JUST TRUE means the requirement is met; JUST FALSE means it is not (a "must" not done: fork: bare-must).
-- src:8700 | Publication
-- src:8701 | (4) Rules of court that are made under this section must be published or otherwise made available to the public.
@ref s 482(4) (src:8700-8701)
GIVEN `the rules of court are made under section 482` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules have been published or otherwise made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the rules of court are made under section 482` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rules of court that are made under this section"
        IF `the rules have been published or otherwise made available to the public` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be published or otherwise made available to the public" (a "must" not done)

-- What the Governor in Council considers proper is a judgment handed to someone else: a plain input (never guessed).
-- src:8702 | Regulations to secure uniformity
-- src:8703 | (5) Notwithstanding anything in this section, the Governor in Council may make such provision as he considers proper to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters, and all uniform rules made under the authority of this subsection prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act.
@ref s 482(5) (src:8702-8703)
GIVEN `the provision is one that the Governor in Council considers proper to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(5) the Governor in Council may make the provision to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one that the Governor in Council considers proper to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such provision as he considers proper to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters"

-- The effect of subsection (5): the uniform rules prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act.
@ref s 482(5) (src:8703)
GIVEN `the rules are uniform rules made under the authority of subsection 482(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482(5) the uniform rules prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act` MEANS
    IF `the rules are uniform rules made under the authority of subsection 482(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all uniform rules made under the authority of this subsection"

§ `Section 482.1 -- Power to make rules respecting case management`

-- The court is the answer of s 482(1) or s 482(2): an input.
-- src:8704 | Power to make rules respecting case management
-- src:8705 | 482.1 (1) A court referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2) may make rules for case management, including rules
-- src:8706 | (a) for the determination of any matter that would assist the court in effective and efficient case management;
-- src:8707 | (b) permitting personnel of the court to deal with administrative matters relating to proceedings out of court; and
-- src:8708 | (c) establishing case management schedules.
@ref s 482.1(1) (src:8704-8708)
DECLARE `s 482.1(1) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 482.1(1)(a) the determination of any matter that would assist the court in effective and efficient case management`
    `s 482.1(1)(b) permitting personnel of the court to deal with administrative matters relating to proceedings out of court`
    `s 482.1(1)(c) establishing case management schedules`
    `s 482.1(1) another matter of case management`

@ref s 482.1(1) (src:8704-8708)
GIVEN `the court is a court referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2), by s 482(1) or s 482(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 482.1(1) the matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court is a court referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2), by s 482(1) or s 482(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the court is one referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2) is not determined
        IF `the court is a court referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2), by s 482(1) or s 482(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2) may make rules for case management"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 482.1(1) another matter of case management` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may make rules for case management, including rules"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JUST TRUE means the party has complied; JUST FALSE that it has not (a "shall" not done: fork: bare-must).
-- src:8709 | Compliance with directions
-- src:8710 | (2) The parties to a case shall comply with any direction made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1).
@ref s 482.1(2) (src:8709-8710)
GIVEN `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has complied with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any direction made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)"
        IF `the party has complied with the direction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The parties to a case shall comply with any direction" (a "shall" not done)

-- A power over the accused;
-- the accused is liable to be compelled. "If rules are made": an "if" on a power: NOT COVERED when unmet (fork: if-on-power).
-- src:8711 | Summons or warrant
-- src:8712 | (3) If rules are made under subsection (1), a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings.
@ref s 482.1(3) (src:8711-8712)
GIVEN `rules are made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person issuing is a court, justice or judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482.1(3) a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `rules are made under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If rules are made under subsection (1)" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)
        IF NOT `the person issuing is a court, justice or judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The provisions that apply are sections 512 and 512.3 (the provision is a Provision of the Code).
-- src:8713 | Provisions to apply
-- src:8714 | (4) Sections 512 and 512.3 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of a summons or a warrant under subsection (3).
@ref s 482.1(4) (src:8713-8714)
GIVEN `the summons or warrant is issued under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summons or warrant is issued under subsection (3)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the issuance of a summons or a warrant under subsection (3)"
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 512 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 512.3 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 512 and 512.3 apply"

-- The provisions that apply are subsections 482(4) and (5).
-- src:8715 | Subsections 482(4) and (5) to apply
-- src:8716 | (5) Subsections 482(4) and (5) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to rules made under subsection (1).
@ref s 482.1(5) (src:8715-8716)
GIVEN `the rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to rules made under subsection (1)"
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 482 AND (`the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(4)" OR `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(5)") THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections 482(4) and (5) apply"

-- No operative text: carried as a quotation.
-- src:8717 | (6) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 187]
@ref s 482.1(6), repealed (src:8717)
`s 482.1(6) as the text shows it` MEANS "(6) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 187]"
